---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import AboutPlainLead from '../../components/AboutPlainLead.astro';
---

<Layout
  title={"Deterministic Null: A Control Experiment for Neural and Agentic Substrates"}
  description={"About: Pre-registered null-model control experiment testing where multi-vendor cloud and local open-weight neural models exceed a zero-call 64-bit integer case loop across exp-001, exp-002, and reviewer-closure suite exp-003."}
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Research study · draft · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      Deterministic Null: A Control Experiment for Neural and Agentic Substrates
    </h1>
    <AboutPlainLead id="deterministic-null" />
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      This study builds and registers an explicit zero-model-call control arm (Shape D: a 64-bit integer loop over a verified append-only case store, implemented across Rust, Go, Python, C++20, and Julia in <a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev/deterministic-null" class="text-brand-cyan">openIE-dev/deterministic-null</a>) and measures the paired completion increment of multi-vendor frontier cloud and local open-weight language models against it under League of Entropy <code>drand</code> public beacons and OpenTimestamps Bitcoin Calendar receipts.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray mb-3">What the study claims and what it does not</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <li>Cross-language determinism (Gate G2): five independent implementations (Rust, Go, Python, C++20, and Julia) agree bit-for-bit on the frozen conformance store digest (<code>0da4df8d9ccbce1e...</code>) and 1,000,000-record <code>DNULLMM1</code> <code>mmap</code> probe checksum (<code>15027705736</code>) with zero floating-point operations inside the loop and zero model calls at decision time.</li>
        <li>Pre-beacon cryptographic registration (Gate G1) &amp; companion closures: Track-A (<code>reg-exp-001</code>, 2,840 instances) and Track-B (<code>reg-exp-002</code>, 1,190 unique instances across Unique 3-SAT, BFCL v3, tau-bench Retail, BigCodeBench v0.1.3, and SWE-bench Verified) lock all store digests, prompts, and sample sizes before target <code>drand</code> rounds exist, while companion suite <code>exp-003</code> adds non-Anthropic cloud breadth (<code>OpenAI gpt-oss-120b</code> <code>+45.83</code> pts, <code>xAI Grok 4.20</code> <code>+44.17</code> pts over <code>N1</code>), resolves <code>formal.unique_3sat_drat</code> via extended thinking (<code>49/50</code>) and 6-turn <code>O(m)</code> clause feedback (<code>50/50</code>, matching standalone <code>CDCL+DRAT</code> <code>B1</code> at <code>$0.00</code>), and verifies real upstream <code>SWE-bench Verified</code> multi-turn GitHub patches + <code>pytest</code> execution (<code>5/6</code> <code>Opus 5.5</code>, <code>5/6</code> <code>0</code>-call replay).</li>
        <li>Two empirical regimes separated by Good–Turing unseen mass: when structural feature cells saturate, frozen Shape D matches or approaches neural completion at zero decision-time model calls; on open compositional synthesis, neural substrates show large positive increments while online crystallization cuts recurring Zipfian model calls and energy by <code>3.59×</code>.</li>
        <li>Not claimed: wall-plug or named-rail hardware joule meter readings (<code>board_metered = false</code>, <code>measured_j = None</code>; local Apple M5 Max counters are on-chip IOReport and kernel <code>ri_energy_nj</code> <code>reported_j</code> values, and closed-API server energy is recorded strictly as <code>not_available</code>), human third-party sealed Tier-3 task authoring, or that any shortfall of a finite store establishes model necessity.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <figure class="mt-10 glass-card p-4 fig-wide">
      <a class="fig-zoom" href="/figures/deterministic-null/dnull-control-protocol.svg" aria-label="Enlarge figure"><img src="/figures/deterministic-null/dnull-control-protocol.svg" alt="Four-stage Deterministic Null pre-beacon lock and paired evaluation protocol. Protocol diagram, not a hardware rail reading." class="fig-img w-full rounded bg-white" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">Pre-beacon registration (<code>Gate G1</code> + OpenTimestamps + <code>drand</code>) and paired evaluation protocol. Protocol diagram, not a rail power reading.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/papers/deterministic-null/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-dark bg-brand-amber px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-gold transition-colors">
        Read → /papers/deterministic-null/
      </a>
      <a href="/pdfs/deterministic-null.pdf" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-amber border border-brand-amber/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-amber/10 transition-colors" download>
        Download PDF
      </a>
      <a href="/living/deterministic-null/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-amber border border-brand-amber/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-amber/10 transition-colors">
        Interactive figures → /living/deterministic-null/
      </a>
      <a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev/deterministic-null" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-cyan border border-brand-cyan/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-cyan/10 transition-colors">
        Repository: openIE-dev/deterministic-null
      </a>
      <a href="/data/#deterministic-null" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-cyan border border-brand-cyan/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-cyan/10 transition-colors">
        Data &amp; digests → /data/#deterministic-null
      </a>
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate border border-brand-border px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:text-brand-white transition-colors">
        ← Catalog
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
